Spec: MitM Maintenance SendMail Job

Platform: Go/Linux

Purpose:
  Scheduled CLI batch utility that processes `*.SendMail` files from a mail outbox directory, dispatches them via SMTP using credentials decrypted from `source_credentials`, manages retry counts and `*.failed` files, and reports outbox health via the scheduler IPC socket.

Structure:
  ./main.go: CLI entry point, IPC client, envelope decryption, header/legacy file parsing, attempt tracking, and SMTP dispatch
  ./main_test.go: Unit tests for KEK validation, envelope decryption, header/legacy parsing, CR/LF rejection, retry/failed handling, permission checks, and recipient masking
  ./build.sh: Static binary build script

Owns:
  ./main.go
  ./main_test.go
  ./go.mod
  ./go.sum
  ./build.sh
  ./README.md
  ./CHANGELOG.md
  ./NOTICE
  ./.gitignore
  @SendMailArgs
  @SourceConfig
  @TargetDBConfig
  @ParsedMail
  @IPCClient
  @validateKEK
  @maskEmail

References:
  ../../collector-layer/collector_concept.md
  ../../collector-layer/collector_creation_guide.md

Must:
  Fetch `MASTER_KEY` and `MITM_DB_CONFIG_JSON` from the scheduler Unix Domain Socket via `get_credentials` at startup, falling back to environment variables for standalone execution.
  Report `status` and `audit` events via a nil-safe `@IPCClient` without writing directly to database log tables.
  Unwrap the active Data Encryption Key from `storage_keys` using the 32-byte KEK (AES-GCM, 12-byte nonce prefix) and decrypt the SMTP configuration from `source_credentials` (`config_payload`) for the configured `source_name`.
  Allow the CLI `mail_dir` argument to override `watch_dir` from `source_credentials`.
  Report a `WARNING:` audit event if `mail_dir` or any processed `*.SendMail` file grants permissions to group or others (`perm & 0o077 != 0`).
  Ignore `*.tmp` and `*.attempts` files when scanning `mail_dir`.
  Support both header-block `*.SendMail` files (`To`, optional `Cc`, `Subject`, optional `X-MitM-*` headers before the first empty line) and legacy `<recipient>.SendMail` files without a header block.
  Accept multiple comma-separated recipients in `To` and `Cc` and forward `X-MitM-*` headers unchanged into the outgoing MIME message.
  Rename a header-block file to `*.failed` and report an `ERROR:` audit event if `To` or `Subject` is missing/invalid or if any header line/value contains CR/LF or control characters.
  Authenticate via SMTP (`AUTH LOGIN` / `PLAIN`) with optional `STARTTLS`; if the SMTP configuration cannot be loaded or the SMTP server connection/authentication fails, emit a `failed` status event and `ERROR:` audit event and exit with code `1` without incrementing per-file attempt counters.
  Track message-level send failures per file in `<name>.attempts` and rename the file to `<name>.failed` with an `ERROR:` audit event once `max_attempts` (default `5`) is reached.
  Delete a `.SendMail` file and its `.attempts` sidecar from disk only after its email has been transmitted without error.
  Report the number of pending `*.SendMail` files, the number of `*.failed` files, and the age of the oldest pending file as an audit event at the end of every run.

Must not:
  Run a persistent filesystem watcher or daemon loop.
  Write email payloads or cursors to `raw_ingestion` or `ingestion_cursors`.
  Include plaintext passwords, keys, mail bodies, or unmasked recipient addresses in logs or IPC events.

Accepts:
  @SendMailArgs: JSON CLI argument in `os.Args[1]` with `source_name`, `mail_dir`, `mail_subject`, `topic`, and `max_attempts`

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Implement `main.go` with scheduler IPC, envelope decryption of `source_credentials`, `*.SendMail` processing, and SMTP transmission.
  [x] #2 Implement unit tests in `main_test.go`.
  [x] #3 Add `build.sh`, `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `NOTICE`, and `.gitignore`.
  [x] #4 Implement Issue #1: header-block parsing (`To`, `Cc`, `Subject`, `X-MitM-*`), CR/LF validation, `.tmp` ignore, `.attempts` & `.failed` handling (`max_attempts`), permission checks, recipient masking, and outbox health reporting.
  [x] #5 Add unit tests for Issue #1 and update `README.md` and `CHANGELOG.md`.

Done when:
  `go test ./...` passes and `build.sh` produces a static binary.

Scenario: header-block mail with multiple recipients and Cc
  Given a `*.SendMail` file with a header block containing two `To` addresses, one `Cc` address, `Subject`, and `X-MitM-Severity`
  When `mitm_maintenance_sendmail` processes the mail directory
  Then the MIME message is sent to all `To` and `Cc` recipients with the header subject and `X-MitM-Severity`
  And the `*.SendMail` file is deleted after transmission

Scenario: legacy mail fallback
  Given a `recipient@example.com.SendMail` file without a header block
  When `mitm_maintenance_sendmail` processes the mail directory
  Then the email is sent to `recipient@example.com` with `mail_subject`
  And the file is deleted after transmission

Scenario: message failure reaches max_attempts
  Given a `*.SendMail` file whose transmission is rejected by the SMTP server `max_attempts` times
  When `mitm_maintenance_sendmail` processes the file on the final attempt
  Then the file is renamed to `*.failed`
  And an `ERROR:` audit event is reported with masked recipient addresses
